<% title "Privacy Policy" %>

<h1 class="heading">Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated 2 August 2026.</p>

<%= render "application/callout", type: "warning", title: "This covers Fuime's pre-launch beta" do %>
  <p class="m0">
    Fuime is not yet handling real money. Payments and cards run against
    Stripe's test mode, so no real funds move through the platform. This policy
    describes what Fuime collects today. Before Fuime handles real money it
    will be replaced by a policy reviewed by a lawyer, and you will be told
    before that happens.
  </p>
<% end %>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>
  Fuime is a financial record-keeping platform for businesses run by teenagers
  aged 13 to 17, with a parent or legal guardian on the account. It is a product
  of <strong><%= Rails.configuration.constants.legal_entity_name %></strong>,
  which is the company responsible for the information described here and the
  one to contact about it. When this policy says &ldquo;we&rdquo; it means
  <%= Rails.configuration.constants.legal_entity_name %>;
  &ldquo;you&rdquo; means anyone with a Fuime account, whether a teen or a
  guardian.
</p>

<h2>Fuime is 13+</h2>
<p>
  You must be at least 13 years old to hold a Fuime account. We ask for a date
  of birth during signup and refuse to create an account for anyone under 13.
  We do not knowingly collect any information from a child under 13. If we
  learn that we have, we delete it. If you believe a child under 13 has given
  us information, email
  <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %> and we will remove it.
</p>

<h2>What we collect</h2>
<p>From everyone with an account:</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    Your name and email address, and your confirmation that you are old enough to
    use Fuime — 13 or older for a founder, 18 or older for a parent or guardian.
    <strong>We do not ask for your date of birth.</strong> We keep the date and
    time you confirmed it, and the IP address and browser you confirmed it from.
  </li>
  <li>
    Security and sign-in information: IP address, browser user agent, login
    times, and any two-factor or security-key credentials you register.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>From a teen running a business:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Business details you enter — name, category, description, storefront text.</li>
  <li>
    Your date of birth, but <em>only</em> if you are issued a Fuime card. Our card
    issuer requires it by law and we cannot issue one without it. If you never get
    a card, we never ask.
  </li>
  <li>
    Transaction records, balances, receipts you upload, and comments you write
    on the ledger.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>From a parent or guardian:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Your name and email address, and your confirmation that you are 18 or older.</li>
  <li>
    A record of your consent: the date and time you accepted the guardian
    agreement, the version of the agreement you accepted, your IP address, and
    your browser user agent. This is what makes your consent auditable, and we
    keep it for as long as the guardianship exists.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Why we collect it</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To run your account and keep it secure.</li>
  <li>
    To enforce the guardian requirement — a teen cannot operate a business on
    Fuime without an active guardian, and we need dates of birth to know who
    that rule applies to.
  </li>
  <li>To keep the books for the business and produce tax summaries.</li>
  <li>To send email you need: sign-in codes, notifications, and receipts.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  We do not sell your information. We do not share it with advertisers. We do
  not use it to train machine-learning models.
</p>

<h2>Who else sees it</h2>
<p>
  A guardian sees everything about the businesses they sign for. That is the
  point of the product and a teen cannot switch it off.
</p>
<p>We also use these companies to run Fuime, and they process data on our behalf:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — payments and card issuing. Currently test mode only.</li>
  <li><strong>Amazon Web Services (S3)</strong> — storage for receipts and uploaded files.</li>
  <li><strong>Render</strong> — application hosting and the database.</li>
  <li><strong>Resend</strong> — outbound email.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  We will also disclose information if the law requires it, or to protect
  someone's safety.
</p>

<h2>If you make your business public</h2>
<p>
  A business can publish a storefront page. When it is public, anyone on the
  internet can see the business name, its description, and its transaction
  history. We deliberately do <em>not</em> publish the account balance, and we
  do not publish the owner's name when the owner is a minor. Publishing is off
  unless someone turns it on, and we recommend a guardian be part of that
  decision.
</p>

<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Account information: as long as the account is open.</li>
  <li>
    Financial records and receipts: seven years, because that is the period tax
    records generally need to be kept for. This applies even after an account
    closes.
  </li>
  <li>
    Everything else: deleted on request, unless we are required to keep it.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Your rights, and a parent's rights</h2>
<p>A parent or guardian on an account may:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Review everything Fuime holds about their teen.</li>
  <li>Withdraw consent, which stops the teen operating a business on Fuime.</li>
  <li>Request that we delete their teen's information.</li>
  <li>Request an export of the business's records.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Email <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %> to make any of these requests.
  Some of them are not yet self-serve in the product; we handle them by hand
  in the meantime, and we do not charge for them.
</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>
  Sensitive fields are encrypted at rest. You can protect your account with
  two-factor authentication or a security key from your
  security settings. If you find a vulnerability, please tell us — see our
  <%= link_to "security page", security_path %>.
</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>
  If we change this policy we will update the date at the top. If a change
  materially affects what we do with your information, we will email you.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
  Questions about this policy, or any request above, go to
  <%= Rails.configuration.constants.legal_entity_name %> at
  <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %>.
</p>

<hr>

<p class="muted">
  See also our <%= link_to "Terms of Service", terms_path %> and the
  <%= link_to "Guardian Agreement", guardian_agreement_path %>.
</p>
